    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="7.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIEm">II Em</ref> 7.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="190" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðonne syððan gebyreð, þæt man sylle ðæs slagan forspecan on hand, ðæt se slaga mote mid griðe nyr ⁊ sylf wæres weddian.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="190" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> syððan gebyreð, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man sylle ðæs slagan forspecan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.2"/> on hand, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> se slaga mote<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.3"/> mid griðe nyr ⁊ sylf wæres<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.4"/> weddian.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="191" ed="#liebermann"/>Deinde oportet, ut prolocutori<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.3-2"/> detur in manu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.4-2"/>, cur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.5"/> interfector audeat accedere cum pace et ipse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.6"/> weram uadiare.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="7.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="10" ed="#robertson"/>Ðonne syððan gebyreð þæt man sylle ðæs slagan forspecan on hand, þæt se slaga mote mid griðe nyr ⁊ sylf wæres<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#IIEm_7-1.robnote.fn.10"/> weddian.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="191" ed="#liebermann"/>Darauf nun gebührt sich, dass man [die beleidigte Sippe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIEm_7-1.lnote.de.1"/>] dem Fürsprech des Todtschlägers in die Hand gelobe, dass der Todtschläger unter [Geleit-]sicherheit näher [kommen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIEm_7-1.lnote.de.2"/>] und selbst sich zu Wergeld[zahlung] rechtsförmlich verpflichten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIEm_7-1.lnote.de.3"/> dürfe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">After that it is fitting that [the injured kindred] give a pledge into the hand of the slayer's advocate that the slayer may [come] nearer under [safe-conduct] protection and himself formally pledge [payment of] the wergild.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="11" ed="#robertson"/>After that it is incumbent upon the kin of the slain man to give security to the slayer’s advocate, that he (the slayer) may approach<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIEm_7-1.robnote.n.1"/> under safe-conduct<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IIEm_7-1.robnote.n.2"/> and pledge himself to pay the wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="430" ed="#whitelock"/>Then afterwards it is fitting that a pledge be given to the slayer’s advocate, that the slayer may approach under safe-conduct and himself pledge to pay the wergild.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Wer_3">Wer 3</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">190</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">forspræcan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">forspræcan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">190</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mot m. griþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mot m. griþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">190</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">weres <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">weres Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">191</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ris <hi rend="italic">Hk;</hi> prael. det. <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ris Hk; prael. det. Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">191</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">manum <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">manum MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">191</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cũ <hi rend="italic">Hk;</hi> quod <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cũ Hk; quod Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIEm_7-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">191</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ipsam <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ipsam Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIEm_7-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">128</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Schiedsgericht 9c</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Schiedsgericht 9c</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIEm_7-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">128</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ellipse des Infinitivs der Bewegung hinter <hi rend="italic">mot</hi>; Beispiele: Toller 699b Ib 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ellipsis of the infinitive of motion after <hi rend="italic">mot</hi>; examples: Toller 699b Ib 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIEm_7-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">128</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘um die Were dingen, sich vertragen’, als gehe ein Feilschen um die Höhe der Zahlung vorher. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Versprechen 3. 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘to bargain about the wergild, come to terms’, as though haggling over the size of the payment came first. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Versprechen 3. 13</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIEm_7-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">297</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The omission of the infinitive of motion is common with <hi rend="italic">mot</hi>, see BT. p. 699, <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> <hi rend="italic">b</hi> (2).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIEm_7-1.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">297</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">Grið</hi> is a Scandinavian loan word. It denotes ‘peace’ in a limited or localised sense, <hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> the sanctuary afforded by special places or the protection granted by a particular person, cf. its compounds <hi rend="italic">ciricgrið</hi> and <hi rend="italic">handgrið</hi>, E. and G. 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIEm_7-1.robnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">10</biblScope></bibl><label>wæres</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">weres</hi> Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
